+- **Read aloud.** Under the light on `/analysis` and `/advisory`, a Listen button reads out the light, the note under it and the page's main sentence and next step, in the page's language. It reads no figure: a sentence with a digit in it is left out. It uses the browser's own speech engine, so nothing is sent anywhere to do it, no model is involved, and it never starts by itself. The button appears only where the browser reports a voice installed on the device for the page's language. A voice the browser reaches over the network is never used, because the sentence would leave the device. **On the owner's Windows laptop (Edge, 29 October 2026) all 321 voices Edge listed were network voices, so no button appears there**; whether a phone browser has an on-device Hindi voice has not been checked. The page has been driven in Edge only against a fake speech engine; the real one has not been run. The button's words and the note under it (the `ra.*` keys) are machine-written in the 7 non-English languages and unreviewed.
+- **The traffic light.** `/analysis`, `/advisory` and `/report` show a green, yellow or red light, drawn as a colour, a shape (circle, triangle, octagon) and a word, so it reads in print and to someone who cannot tell the colours apart. The backend picks it from what it has already worked out (`mvp_summary.band`): green when nothing is flagged (profitable, feasible, low repayment pressure, no money missing, the household within its limit), red when the plan makes no profit, the repayment pressure is high or the household is over its limit, yellow for everything else. It reads only the figures the reader typed, and the note under it says so: it is not a decision about a loan or a scheme, and green does not mean the reader qualifies for anything. Python only, no model. A result stored before the light existed keeps the earlier mark. The rule is the author's own and has not been checked by anyone else.
+- **Simple or Detailed.** `/analysis` and `/advisory` open with a two-button switch, "How much to show". Simple keeps the light, the verdict, the four headline figures and the next steps on `/analysis`, and the light, the main point, the action plan and (with the helper on) the written-plan card on `/advisory`. Detailed shows everything else too: the working, the market prices, the observations, the government support, the loan options, the scheme funding and the registrations. The page opens in Simple, because most of the people this is for read little. A reader who never presses Detailed therefore does not see the loan options, the scheme funding, the registrations or the local prices; the note under the switch says there is more. The choice is a display setting like the language and the theme: it is kept in `localStorage` (`sih-detail`) only once a button has been pressed, and never with the answers. The hidden sections are removed from the page, not folded, so a screen reader skips them too. `/schemes`, `/report` and the printout of `/report` are not affected.
